        "## Summary\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.callout-tip}\n",
        "## Key points\n",
        "\n",
        "- Logistic regression is used for binary outcomes.\n",
        "- It models the **log-odds** as a linear function of the predictors.\n",
        "- The fitted probabilities are always between $0$ and $1$.\n",
        "- A coefficient $\\beta_j$ is interpreted through the odds ratio $e^{\\beta_j}$.\n",
        "- The model is estimated by maximum likelihood rather than least squares.\n",
        "- In Python, `statsmodels` is convenient for classical statistical output, while `sklearn` is convenient for prediction pipelines and classification workflows.\n",
